{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":227,"code_snippet":"ln -s \"${MAIN}/${d}\" \"${wt}/${d}\"","reasoning_trace":"Traced link_deps: DEP_DIRS from the live tree are symlinked into both worktrees by default (LINK_DEPS=1). Built a repo with a venv carrying an __editable__.pkg.pth naming <repo>/src; red = failing test + buggy add, green = fix, live = green. Run reported DECOY (exit 3) and 'pkg imported from <live>/src/pkg/__init__.py'; --no-link-deps reported NOT_A_RED (exit 127).","finding":"Default dependency linking makes red and green runs execute the live working copy whenever a linked directory carries a back-reference, so the gate certifies runs that never exercised the two commits.","critique":"The reviewing skill (SKILL.md:219) cites this output as proof of 'Test fails with current code' and micro-sprint.md:43 makes exit 0 an acceptance criterion.","remediation":"Opt-in --link-deps, or refuse to link directories with back-references (*.pth, workspace symlinks), or probe the resolved module path and fail closed when outside the worktree; add RTC cases.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-706","CWE-345"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/skills/reviewing-code/SKILL.md","line":6,"code_snippet":"Bash(.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh *)","reasoning_trace":"Compared base and head allowed-tools; the new glob wraps a script that execs everything after -- verbatim (red-test-check.sh:248,250) and runs the whitespace-split --setup string (:113,:292), with the reviewer's environment and no prompt. Phase 2 (:219) tells the reviewer to take the command from reviewer.md, written by the engineer under review. Both dissent voices rated this HIGH.","finding":"The review role, declared as State-Zone-only, gains unprompted arbitrary command execution steered by engineer-authored content.","critique":"A prompt-injected or obedient review agent can be made to run any command, exfiltrate credentials, or rewrite the gate's own artefacts.","remediation":"Read the test command from committed config or a runner allowlist; refuse ad-hoc argv in review mode; drop --setup from the review path; document the surface at :7.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-78","CWE-269","OWASP-LLM01:2025"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":227,"code_snippet":"git -C \"$MAIN\" -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null worktree add --detach","reasoning_trace":"Worktrees share the main .git; only the script's own worktree add is hook-protected. A red-commit test running 'git config core.hooksPath /nonexistent/evil-hooks' left the live repo config changed after the run.","finding":"Code at the red commit persists into the live environment via linked dependency directories and the shared .git config.","remediation":"Opt-in linking; pin core.hooksPath/core.fsmonitor via -c and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null for the run; diff .git/config after each run.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-668","CWE-829"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":885,"code_snippet":"if ($0 ~ /^\\|[[:space:]:|-]+$/) { sep = 1 } else if (sep) { rows++ }","reasoning_trace":"Fed a plan dated 2026-10-20 whose Seams block held only the template's {placeholder} row; validator exited 0 with no seams WARN.","finding":"The Seams Under Test hard gate is satisfied by the unedited template placeholder row.","remediation":"Skip rows whose cells are all {…} placeholders/empty; add a SEAMS case.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":180,"reasoning_trace":"RTC-14 pins a test-only green as exit 0 with a stderr WARN; --json object (:136-142) has no warnings field; micro-sprint.md:43 says 'exits 0'.","finding":"A test-only green is invisible to --json consumers and satisfies the acceptance criterion while weakening the test.","remediation":"Distinct TEST_ONLY verdict/exit code or a warnings field in the JSON.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-684"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":275,"reasoning_trace":"On the no-timeout path wait returns when the direct child dies from TERM and the watcher is killed before its KILL; cleanup sends one TERM and removes directories without waiting.","finding":"Timeout escalation and cleanup do not finish killing the run's process group.","remediation":"Wait for the watcher when the timed-out flag exists; poll then KILL in cleanup; prune again after scratch removal.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-404"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":183,"reasoning_trace":"Scratch under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}; this sandbox's /tmp is noexec; a script test command exits 126 at both commits and reads NOT_A_RED.","finding":"A noexec temp filesystem turns a legitimate red into NOT_A_RED.","remediation":"Scratch under $MAIN/.git with TMPDIR fallback; name the cause on exit 126 + Permission denied.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-703"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":52,"reasoning_trace":"Pattern list lacks pytest setup errors, unittest loader failures and jest 'Test suite failed to run'.","finding":"A red that never reached its assertion can read as an assertion failure.","remediation":"Add the three shapes with RTC cases; prefer structured runner output.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":248,"reasoning_trace":"Only GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_PREFIX are unset before exec.","finding":"Red-commit code inherits the operator's full environment including provider keys.","remediation":"Offer --clean-env and have the review skill pass it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-526"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"access_control","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.github/workflows/check-glossary-terms.yml","line":16,"reasoning_trace":"No permissions block; checkout SHA verified as v4.3.1 via the GitHub API.","finding":"Workflow runs with default GITHUB_TOKEN scope.","remediation":"permissions: contents: read","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-250"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":1297,"reasoning_trace":"'A read/write check, e.g. a hook. It asks first.' rejected as 3 sentences.","finding":"Sentence counter counts abbreviations.","remediation":"Neutralise e.g./i.e./etc./vs. or count [.!?] +[A-Z] boundaries.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
{"id":"CQ-007","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":1287,"reasoning_trace":"'read/write' drew the path WARN.","finding":"Path heuristic warns on ordinary slashed prose.","remediation":"Require a path-like shape.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
{"id":"CQ-008","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":871,"reasoning_trace":"'**Date:** October 20, 2026' read as undated; hard rule became a WARN with exit 0.","finding":"A non-ISO header date silently downgrades the seams hard rule.","remediation":"Violation when a Date line exists but no ISO date parses.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
